---
/**
 * The Honor Code itself, the four principles from the Kickoff slides in the
 * group's own words. Shown on /honor-code, and on /slack before the invite,
 * so the wording lives in one place.
 */
---
<ul class="honor">
  <li>
    <strong>Radical Inclusivity.</strong> AI safety is an intimidating field, especially for
    people who don’t have the background or resources to break in. We believe in inviting
    everyone to attend our events.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Community-First Collaboration.</strong> We all succeed by lifting each other up,
    sharing our resources, and creating a strong, welcoming network of peers and mentors.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Rigorous Open-mindedness.</strong> Because the field is so new, common notions of
    AI safety in theory and practice may clash across different people. We believe in
    keeping an open mind to strange ideas that may surprise us.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Proactive Responsibility.</strong> We honor what we say we will do. Lastly, we
    take reports of harassment, discrimination, and dishonesty seriously and have a
    zero-tolerance policy for it.
  </li>
</ul>

<style>
  .honor li + li { margin-block-start: 1rem; }
</style>
